WEBVTT

00:09:58.116 --> 00:10:01.916
I don't want it to sound like a magic act,
but Lily and I don't know each other.

00:10:01.956 --> 00:10:03.796
We haven't gone through this before,

00:10:03.836 --> 00:10:05.916
but what I want to try to do is actually,

00:10:05.956 --> 00:10:08.116
the hearing of the stories
of people's regrets

00:10:08.156 --> 00:10:10.156
I think is super
interesting and revealing.

00:10:10.196 --> 00:10:12.356
We’re going to hear Lily’s regret,

00:10:12.396 --> 00:10:14.956
and we're going to talk through
what science says

00:10:14.996 --> 00:10:18.236
might be some appropriate
responses to that.

00:10:18.276 --> 00:10:19.916
So, Lily, welcome.

00:10:19.956 --> 00:10:21.436
Lily: Thank you, hi everyone.

00:10:21.756 --> 00:10:23.596
DHP: And tell us where you are.

00:10:24.356 --> 00:10:26.436
L: I'm currently in Brooklyn, New York.

00:10:26.996 --> 00:10:30.196
DHP: Brooklyn is in the house
here at TED Membership.